3.1 Foundational Regularity Conditions

Before specifying the coupled dynamics, we establish the regularity conditions under which the HALSC system is well-posed. These conditions are verified for each architectural component in Chapter 4.

Assumption 3.1 (Regularity Conditions).

1. The forgetting kernel \kappa: [0,T] \times [0,T] \to \mathbb{R}_+ is C^1 in both arguments with uniformly bounded partial derivatives \|\partial_t \kappa\|_\infty \leq K_\kappa and \|\partial_\tau \kappa\|_\infty \leq K_\kappa.
2. The environmental forcing E: [0,T] \to \mathcal{E}_{\text{env}} is piecewise C^1 with at most finitely many jump discontinuities, each of finite magnitude.
3. All neural network components (embedding functions, salience networks, TPE drift and diffusion networks) are parameterized with spectral norm bounds enforced via gradient clipping: there exists L_{\text{nn}} > 0 such that for any neural component f_\theta, we have \|f_\theta(x) - f_\theta(y)\| \leq L_{\text{nn}}\|x - y\| for all x, y in the relevant domain.
