· W_H, W_A are independent standard Wiener processes on \mathcal{H}, \mathcal{A} respectively.
· \sigma_H, \sigma_A are the diffusion coefficient fields.

The crucial structural property is the coupling:

\frac{\partial f}{\partial A} \not\equiv 0, \qquad \frac{\partial g}{\partial H} \not\equiv 0 \tag{3.3}

This bidirectional coupling distinguishes HALSC from all prior personalization frameworks.

